1
00:00:15,098 --> 00:00:19,853
June 5th, 1972.

2
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:23,898
On a hot humid night,
deep in the southern United States,

3
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:28,903
one baby let out his first cry
in a hospital.

4
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:33,992
However, this baby took his last breath
in his mother's arms

5
00:00:34,075 --> 00:00:37,746
before even seeing the first light of day.

6
00:00:38,329 --> 00:00:41,875
Until this point in her life,
this young mother had a hard life,

7
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:45,003
and felt hopelessly miserable.

8
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:50,258
This baby had become
her only pride and joy,

9
00:00:50,341 --> 00:00:53,720
and her only hope for a bright future.

10
00:00:54,304 --> 00:00:58,141
Thus, she refused
to accept the baby's death.

11
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:03,521
Before the doctor and the nurses
saw that the baby died,

12
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:07,525
the mother slipped out of her bed
like a ghost.

13
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:11,237
She found another baby
born on the same day,

14
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:13,823
and left her dead baby in its place.

15
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:15,617
She then kept the baby as her own.

16
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:20,538
The swapped baby had a fraternal twin.

17
00:01:21,247 --> 00:01:24,542
She was never questioned,

18
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:27,462
and no one suspected foul play.

19
00:01:31,674 --> 00:01:34,093
Mommy, whose grave is this?

20
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:35,929
That's my birthday.

21
00:01:37,138 --> 00:01:38,264
He died the same day?

22
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:39,808
Enrico,

23
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:45,230
you had a younger brother.

24
00:01:45,814 --> 00:01:47,649
He was your twin,

25
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:51,861
but he died at the hospital
moments after you were born.

26
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:54,697
Pray for him.

27
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:56,908
After his passing,

28
00:01:57,992 --> 00:02:00,829
we named him Domenic.

29
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:05,250
1987

30
00:02:06,084 --> 00:02:08,545
Oh Lord, answer my plea.

31
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:12,298
My brother passed away
on the day we were born.

32
00:02:13,341 --> 00:02:17,554
Why did fate choose him and not me?

33
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:21,891
Why… must there be
happiness and misfortune?

34
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:24,811
What is true happiness?

35
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:29,149
Father Pucchi was
15 years old at the time.

36
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:33,236
His paternal grandmother
was an Italian immigrant.

37
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:38,241
She came from a family with ties
to a prestigious clan in Venice

38
00:02:38,324 --> 00:02:41,536
which hailed a well-known clergyman
in the 18th century.

39
00:02:41,619 --> 00:02:44,956
When the young man showed interest
in pursuing priesthood,

40
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:47,792
no one spoke out against this decision.

41
00:02:53,339 --> 00:02:56,467
What did you do? Who are you?

42
00:02:58,303 --> 00:03:00,263
What are you doing here?

43
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:02,223
Hey!

44
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:03,683
Is this your book?

45
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:08,187
This is a famous autobiography of a cleric
who had an affair with a married woman.

46
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:11,274
He later left the church
and became a painter.

47
00:03:11,357 --> 00:03:15,236
Do clergymen read such books?

48
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:18,489
Who are you, and how did you get inside?

49
00:03:18,573 --> 00:03:22,952
This ossuary is closed to the public
except on Sundays.

50
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:28,833
You see, I'm allergic to sunlight.

51
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:32,795
The sun won't set until 6:19 p.m. tonight.

52
00:03:33,379 --> 00:03:35,089
I'm unable to leave until then,

53
00:03:35,173 --> 00:03:37,050
so that's why I was resting here.

54
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:41,346
All right.

55
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:44,224
Is there anything I can do for you?

56
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:46,059
No.

57
00:03:46,142 --> 00:03:47,310
I see.

58
00:03:48,102 --> 00:03:49,187
I pity you.

59
00:03:50,855 --> 00:03:53,024
I won't tell Father about this,

60
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:55,360
so you should leave at sunset.

61
00:03:58,863 --> 00:04:01,282
You're an interesting fellow.

62
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:04,285
What's that?

63
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:06,079
You won't force me to leave?

64
00:04:06,162 --> 00:04:11,000
I could be a thief who snuck in
to steal the artwork here,

65
00:04:11,084 --> 00:04:12,669
or even worse.

66
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:15,546
Or maybe you're just
saying that I can stay,

67
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:18,216
but you're going to report me.

68
00:04:18,299 --> 00:04:19,759
Is that your wish?

69
00:04:21,135 --> 00:04:25,098
No thief would lie and say
that they're allergic to sunlight.

70
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:28,393
Not even the devil
would tell a lie like that.

71
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:30,228
Hold on.

72
00:04:30,311 --> 00:04:32,146
Did you sprain your ankle?

73
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:34,482
Was that my fault? Are you hurt?

74
00:04:34,565 --> 00:04:35,942
Oh, no.

75
00:04:36,025 --> 00:04:39,028
It's not your fault. I was born with this.

76
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:42,615
My left toes are bent,

77
00:04:42,699 --> 00:04:45,451
but I can walk around just fine.

78
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:51,291
Do you believe in the force of gravity?

79
00:04:51,791 --> 00:04:55,586
You tripped on me for a reason.

80
00:04:57,755 --> 00:04:59,299
What are you saying?

81
00:05:04,679 --> 00:05:08,099
Take this stone arrowhead.

82
00:05:08,182 --> 00:05:12,103
If you have no use for it, that's fine.

83
00:05:12,812 --> 00:05:16,274
But isn't it gravity
that draws people to each other?

84
00:05:16,858 --> 00:05:21,279
I don't know
what impression you have of me,

85
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:24,532
but I travel to meet people.

86
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:28,369
If you ever wish to see me again,

87
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:32,332
wish upon this arrow and call me.

88
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:35,043
No matter how far in the future
that may be.

89
00:05:35,543 --> 00:05:36,586
Do you understand?

90
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:39,297
Just keep me in your back burner.

91
00:05:40,965 --> 00:05:42,508
At sunset,

92
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:44,969
I will leave.

93
00:05:54,353 --> 00:05:55,938
What's this?

94
00:05:56,689 --> 00:05:59,400
My foot! The toes!

95
00:05:59,984 --> 00:06:01,736
They're straight!

96
00:06:02,236 --> 00:06:04,572
Wait! Who are you?

97
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:10,953
1988

98
00:06:11,829 --> 00:06:13,206
Father.

99
00:06:14,749 --> 00:06:15,750
Please hear me out.

100
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:19,670
I must confess my sins.

101
00:06:20,254 --> 00:06:21,589
Sorry,

102
00:06:21,672 --> 00:06:23,174
let me go get the priest…

103
00:06:23,257 --> 00:06:27,512
My body is stricken with an illness.

104
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:30,848
I don't have much longer.

105
00:06:31,557 --> 00:06:35,645
But my confession
isn't about this illness.

106
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:39,440
It concerns my family.

107
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:44,070
It was 16 years ago, on June 5th.

108
00:06:44,153 --> 00:06:48,866
My baby died,
so I took another woman's baby,

109
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:54,580
and swapped the two babies
while no one was looking.

110
00:06:54,664 --> 00:06:56,582
I took one of the twins.

111
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:03,089
I cannot express how terrible I feel
for the baby's mother.

112
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:08,177
But I poured my heart
into raising this baby.

113
00:07:09,053 --> 00:07:10,805
I had a happy life.

114
00:07:10,888 --> 00:07:14,892
He grew up to be a great boy.

115
00:07:16,185 --> 00:07:19,188
Shouldn't I tell him that
he has a twin brother

116
00:07:20,064 --> 00:07:24,360
before I leave this world?

117
00:07:24,444 --> 00:07:26,863
What if I tell him the truth,

118
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:29,615
and my son leaves me before I die?

119
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:33,161
So…

120
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:35,913
Do you know the other family?

121
00:07:36,873 --> 00:07:40,460
They live in a large estate
in the neighboring town.

122
00:07:41,502 --> 00:07:43,921
The couple's name is Pucchi.

123
00:07:46,924 --> 00:07:48,134
Seriously?

124
00:07:48,217 --> 00:07:51,137
What's so good about a juice delivery boy?

125
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,138
Gross.

126
00:07:52,221 --> 00:07:53,473
I bet he's a coward.

127
00:07:53,556 --> 00:07:57,226
- I love that.
- Forget him, his family's probably poor.

128
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:59,187
He doesn't even go to high school.

129
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:01,230
That's why he works.

130
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,525
Perla, isn't that your bag?

131
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:06,235
He snatched it!

132
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:07,945
Thief!

133
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:09,614
Someone stop him!

134
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:19,332
- Woo-hoo!
- Yes!

135
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:21,918
Oh, crap!

136
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:24,795
I broke the store window.

137
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:27,423
I'll get fired from
this part-time delivery job.

138
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:30,092
My school doesn't even allow
students to work.

139
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:34,514
Weather Forecast's real name
is Wes Aquamarine.

140
00:08:35,139 --> 00:08:37,016
He was 16 at the time.

141
00:08:37,099 --> 00:08:39,227
He was innocent
in every sense of the word,

142
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,729
and he relentlessly pursued justice.

143
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:44,690
Well… Thanks.

144
00:08:45,274 --> 00:08:46,901
That was my bag he tried to steal.

145
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:51,197
I'll tell everyone that
the thief smashed the window.

146
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:53,908
- Really?
- Of course.

147
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:55,493
Now go.

148
00:08:59,121 --> 00:09:01,290
I'm Wes.

149
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:02,959
People call me Weather.

150
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:05,586
Can I see you again?

151
00:09:10,591 --> 00:09:14,136
Two months have passed
since that confession.

152
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:16,931
Father Pucchi was under distress.

153
00:09:18,057 --> 00:09:20,768
Though not yet appointed a priest,

154
00:09:20,851 --> 00:09:24,480
he is obliged to keep the privacy
of the believers.

155
00:09:25,481 --> 00:09:27,942
He must keep the confession a secret.

156
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:29,944
Otherwise,

157
00:09:30,027 --> 00:09:33,322
he would be deemed unworthy
as a clergyman.

158
00:09:34,031 --> 00:09:38,869
That mother wants to
take her secret to her grave.

159
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:42,623
Had I been able to
convince her to tell the truth,

160
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:47,086
how will we cope,
and how will my younger brother react?

161
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:50,089
Will we be able to
treat our families the same?

162
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:53,509
I'm home.

163
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:55,678
Welcome back.

164
00:09:55,761 --> 00:09:58,556
Why are you spaced out on the porch?

165
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:00,808
Did something happen at school?

166
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:04,061
Please, Enrico.

167
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:07,440
Don't tell Mom and Dad about this!

168
00:10:07,523 --> 00:10:08,357
What?

169
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:10,443
My grades are slipping.

170
00:10:10,526 --> 00:10:13,112
I'll make up for it,
but there's something on my mind.

171
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:18,492
I'm dating someone.

172
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:21,704
We met only two weeks ago,

173
00:10:21,787 --> 00:10:23,205
but I really like him.

174
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:27,460
It's like our hearts are connected.
I've never felt like this.

175
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,172
I'm happy for you, Perla.

176
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:34,091
Enrico…

177
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:37,053
Let me tell you how this went.

178
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:40,556
Father Pucchi never told his sister Perla,

179
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:44,894
that Weather was their biological brother.

180
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:50,775
I want you to judge
the rest of the events.

181
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:54,445
Who committed a sin?

182
00:10:55,029 --> 00:10:57,823
Is it the mother, who swapped the babies?

183
00:10:57,907 --> 00:10:59,200
Or is it Father Pucchi's parents?

184
00:10:59,283 --> 00:11:00,868
Is it Father Pucchi?

185
00:11:01,494 --> 00:11:04,121
Is it the younger brother Weather,
who knows nothing?

186
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:08,959
Father Pucchi looked into Weather,
the man his sister loved.

187
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:13,047
After learning the shocking truth,

188
00:11:13,130 --> 00:11:14,965
Father Pucchi had only one choice to make.

189
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:20,221
I can't let my sister get hurt,
no matter what!

190
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:27,478
You're that wealthy kid
who goes to divinity school.

191
00:11:27,978 --> 00:11:30,147
Should you be doing this?

192
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:32,650
If you succeed, I'll give you double.

193
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:34,860
I have two requests.

194
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:37,446
One, do not ask any questions.

195
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:40,449
Two, make them break up.

196
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:43,869
If I can get some thugs to threaten Wes,

197
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:45,955
he'll break up with my sister.

198
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:48,958
That's all Perla will experience,

199
00:11:49,041 --> 00:11:51,627
nothing but an ordinary heartbreak.

200
00:11:51,710 --> 00:11:54,547
This won't leave a permanent scar.

201
00:11:55,589 --> 00:11:57,716
However, Father Pucchi
barely knew anything

202
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:02,179
about this private investigator,
a jack of all trades.

203
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:06,642
How keen he was to information,
nor the darkness he carried.

204
00:12:06,725 --> 00:12:12,857
It is the darkness this society had,
which was allowed by law a century ago.

205
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:15,109
It is a despicable old history.

206
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:22,283
I can't believe what I learned
about Wes's birth.

207
00:12:22,867 --> 00:12:27,288
In 1972, his mother married

208
00:12:27,371 --> 00:12:29,665
a black man in the city.

209
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:33,377
That makes him the son of a black man.

210
00:12:35,504 --> 00:12:39,175
The private detective
gathered other zealots.

211
00:12:40,676 --> 00:12:42,219
Weather!

212
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:44,346
Perla…

213
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:51,812
What are you doing? You're all drunk!

214
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:53,522
We won't hurt you.

215
00:12:53,606 --> 00:12:55,566
He's the one we need to punish.

216
00:12:55,649 --> 00:12:59,195
Come give me a kiss.

217
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:02,406
One for this officer too!

218
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:05,117
You're a whore pretending to be
a proper little missy.

219
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:08,662
Fool around with whomever you want,

220
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:13,792
but this bastard isn't allowed
to kiss you, not even a little.

221
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:20,591
Your brother wanted this done.

222
00:13:21,842 --> 00:13:25,930
And as for the woman
who gave birth to you,

223
00:13:26,013 --> 00:13:30,017
we set her house on fire.

224
00:13:42,446 --> 00:13:46,700
Who was the one truly being punished?

225
00:13:47,701 --> 00:13:50,663
Was it Weather, Perla, or…

226
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:54,375
They all tried to love in their own ways.

227
00:13:55,584 --> 00:13:57,169
These are the facts.

228
00:13:57,753 --> 00:14:00,965
Father Pucchi's love
brought the worst outcome.

229
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:06,053
Weather was hung high
on a tree by a cliff,

230
00:14:06,136 --> 00:14:08,055
and left to die.

231
00:14:08,847 --> 00:14:11,433
Perla truly had a pure heart,

232
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:15,938
which was filled with a soft breeze
until this moment.

233
00:14:16,021 --> 00:14:18,357
Their love was like the warm spring sun.

234
00:14:19,108 --> 00:14:20,025
However…

235
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:27,825
In my heart,

236
00:14:29,201 --> 00:14:31,954
there will never be another drop of rain.

237
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:34,915
And with those words,

238
00:14:35,499 --> 00:14:38,752
Perla threw herself down
into the lake below the cliff.

239
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:43,883
She did not know
that Weather had a slight pulse.

240
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:56,186
Why?

241
00:14:56,854 --> 00:14:58,689
How could this happen?

242
00:15:00,232 --> 00:15:03,611
Why did I pursue the path of priesthood?

243
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:06,363
Why do people meet?

244
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:08,032
Had they never met,

245
00:15:08,115 --> 00:15:10,534
this would have never happened.

246
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:12,536
No!

247
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:18,834
Stop that!

248
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:22,296
Don't make the sign of the cross
at my sister!

249
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:26,967
Dammit.

250
00:15:27,551 --> 00:15:31,138
Please, just don't take Perla's life!

251
00:15:31,221 --> 00:15:32,890
Perla is innocent.

252
00:15:32,973 --> 00:15:35,100
She only fell in love!

253
00:15:35,184 --> 00:15:38,812
I'll do anything to bring her back!

254
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:43,692
I'm the one who should be punished!

255
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:46,195
Do you believe in the force of gravity?

256
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:49,239
We met for a reason.

257
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:52,534
If you wish,

258
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:55,329
come see me.

259
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,039
It's him.

260
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:59,667
That was his voice.

261
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,251
I want to see him.

262
00:16:01,335 --> 00:16:05,881
He once healed my bent toes
in the ossuary.

263
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:09,385
Why did I forget about him until now?

264
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:12,262
That's right, he gave me…

265
00:16:12,846 --> 00:16:15,224
an arrowhead-like thing.

266
00:16:22,064 --> 00:16:24,984
What is going on?

267
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:28,946
The arrowhead in my pocket?

268
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:31,281
Once a life is lost,

269
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:33,909
you cannot bring it back.

270
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:36,161
But it's up to you.

271
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:38,497
If you wish from deep within your heart,

272
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:41,792
you can retrieve her memory.

273
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:44,294
It's the memories of her heart.

274
00:16:44,878 --> 00:16:47,339
This is your awakening.

275
00:16:59,184 --> 00:17:01,103
Who the hell are you?

276
00:17:01,186 --> 00:17:04,606
The idiot who wanted
an affair investigated?

277
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:08,110
If you don't want to get shot,
show your dirty face--

278
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:11,238
What's this?

279
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:13,949
If you know, then tell me.

280
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,075
What?

281
00:17:15,159 --> 00:17:16,952
I heard you know everything.

282
00:17:17,536 --> 00:17:20,456
What made these snails emerge
out of the blue?

283
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:23,250
Where do they come from?

284
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:25,878
Why is it only happening near me?

285
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:28,255
Who the hell are you?

286
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:31,425
You said Perla's brother
asked you to split us.

287
00:17:31,508 --> 00:17:32,676
Is that true?

288
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:35,012
No, you can't be…

289
00:17:38,682 --> 00:17:42,436
What are these snails?

290
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:49,860
Damn. I knew it, I can't die.

291
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:54,656
The gunpowder is soaked.

292
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:56,700
But only when I try to shoot myself.

293
00:17:57,701 --> 00:17:59,828
Why am I still alive?

294
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:03,373
Weather was full of rage.

295
00:18:03,957 --> 00:18:07,086
He was enraged at those
who persecuted him,

296
00:18:07,836 --> 00:18:10,047
at the fact that he was alive,

297
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:14,301
and that he couldn't save Perla.

298
00:18:16,053 --> 00:18:18,722
Once Weather learned about Perla's death,

299
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:20,641
he jumped off the cliff.

300
00:18:21,225 --> 00:18:23,602
Just then,
there was a strong gust of wind.

301
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:28,774
He also tried to drown himself
in the lake,

302
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:31,985
but the waves brought him back to shore.

303
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:36,990
Why won't you let me die with Perla?

304
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:47,459
His anger was one of despair.

305
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:52,714
His vengeance spread to all,
not just to the townspeople.

306
00:18:55,008 --> 00:18:56,468
On the fourth night,

307
00:18:56,552 --> 00:18:59,596
a horde of snails swarmed the town.

308
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:02,015
Why snails?

309
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:04,101
Where did they come from?

310
00:19:04,184 --> 00:19:06,812
No one knew.

311
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:09,982
The only one who understood
the cause of this incident

312
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:14,153
was Father Pucchi,
who woke up in a hospital.

313
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:17,406
Wes… no, Weather did this.

314
00:19:17,489 --> 00:19:19,366
My brother isn't dead.

315
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:21,326
We are twins.

316
00:19:21,410 --> 00:19:24,496
My awakening led to his.

317
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:30,335
Just as I sought her memory,
so did Weather, though subconsciously.

318
00:19:30,919 --> 00:19:34,715
If these snails are here to
crawl up my arm,

319
00:19:34,798 --> 00:19:37,342
then I have to go kill my brother.

320
00:19:38,635 --> 00:19:41,096
I will resort to any and every method
from now on.

321
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:43,265
I will even take lives.

322
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:46,935
Once my score with Weather is settled,

323
00:19:47,019 --> 00:19:48,812
I will go see him.

324
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:51,273
His name is Dio.

325
00:19:51,815 --> 00:19:54,067
Why do people's paths cross?

326
00:19:54,151 --> 00:19:56,653
If anyone can tell me, it's him.

327
00:19:57,696 --> 00:19:58,864
I must know it.

328
00:19:58,947 --> 00:20:03,035
The answer to this question
is the strongest power in this world.

329
00:20:03,619 --> 00:20:05,245
It must also be the truth.

330
00:20:09,416 --> 00:20:10,500
Are you satisfied?

331
00:20:11,043 --> 00:20:14,838
Your sister Perla died
because of your request.

332
00:20:15,339 --> 00:20:16,173
And…

333
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:18,675
I can't suppress my rage.

334
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:20,844
We have a score to settle.

335
00:20:21,428 --> 00:20:22,512
You're wrong.

336
00:20:22,596 --> 00:20:25,390
It's because I am your older brother.

337
00:20:26,558 --> 00:20:29,019
But that ends today.

338
00:20:29,102 --> 00:20:32,314
Weather, meet your end.

339
00:20:38,695 --> 00:20:41,740
Weather, you are in my way.

340
00:20:42,324 --> 00:20:43,450
Now die,

341
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:45,744
and take those rainbows with you.

342
00:20:45,827 --> 00:20:49,790
Vanish with Perla and all your memories.

343
00:20:50,374 --> 00:20:53,961
A man with no memories
might as well be dead.

344
00:20:54,044 --> 00:20:58,131
Live as if you're dead trapped in a cage.

345
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:07,641
Inmate MA152403.

346
00:21:08,141 --> 00:21:09,476
Imprisoned!

347
00:21:12,062 --> 00:21:14,564
My sole purpose in life

348
00:21:14,648 --> 00:21:16,984
is to settle my score with him.

349
00:21:18,026 --> 00:21:20,862
So you've been revived.

350
00:21:20,946 --> 00:21:22,656
Your memories returned!

351
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:26,827
But I thought you were
going to meet up with Jolyne!

352
00:21:27,869 --> 00:21:31,498
I'm only with you to find Jolyne!

353
00:21:31,581 --> 00:21:33,834
You shouldn't go find Jolyne.

354
00:21:33,917 --> 00:21:35,502
It'll be a waste of time.

355
00:21:35,585 --> 00:21:36,545
Moreover,

356
00:21:36,628 --> 00:21:39,214
I need someone to finish me off.

357
00:21:40,882 --> 00:21:42,175
Kill me.

358
00:21:42,884 --> 00:21:45,137
I'm counting on you, Anastasia.

359
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,640
That's why these beetles are called
snail eaters!

360
00:21:48,724 --> 00:21:51,268
These buggers!

361
00:21:56,773 --> 00:21:57,691
Get in, guys!

362
00:21:59,901 --> 00:22:01,903
They're coming in through the cracks!

363
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:03,322
What do we do, Jolyne?

364
00:22:03,905 --> 00:22:06,491
Whether inside or outside the car,

365
00:22:06,575 --> 00:22:09,828
it's over once we get devoured.

366
00:22:10,412 --> 00:22:13,165
We'll go meet up with Weather
as we're being eaten!

367
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:46,299
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
